      "title": "NSW Greens MP pleads with federal colleagues not to back National party motion to block koala park deal",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/nsw-greens-mp-pleads-with-federal-colleagues-not-to-not-to-back-national-party-motion-to-block-koala-park",
      "description": "<p>Federal Greens partyroom split over plan for NSW to get millions of dollars’ worth in carbon credits for creating a koala national park</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/08/barnaby-joyce-one-nation-superannuation-plan-john-howard-immigration-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A New South Wales Greens MP has pleaded with her federal colleagues not to vote with the Coalition and One Nation to block a plan for the NSW government to get millions of dollars’ worth in carbon credits for creating a koala national park.</p><p>Sue Higginson, a former lawyer and forest campaigner turned NSW upper house MP, is the first member of the minor party to speak in detail about a dispute that has split the Greens and environmentalists.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/nsw-greens-mp-pleads-with-federal-colleagues-not-to-not-to-back-national-party-motion-to-block-koala-park\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T22:06:49"
    },
    {
      "title": "Stolen Generations survivors have more health challenges than other First Nations people",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/stolen-generations-survivors-have-more-health-challenges-than-other-first-nations-people-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Indigenous Australians forcibly removed under government policies more likely to have severe or profound disability, report finds</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/08/barnaby-joyce-one-nation-superannuation-plan-john-howard-immigration-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The tens of thousands of Indigenous Australians and their descendants who were forcibly removed under government assimilation policies have far greater physical and health challenges when compared with the wider Indigenous and non-Indigenous populations, according to a new report.</p><p>The report by the Australian Institute of Health and Welfare (AIHW) was commissioned by peak advocacy body the Healing Foundation, which supports Stolen Generations survivors and their families, and builds on existing data released in 2023.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/stolen-generations-survivors-have-more-health-challenges-than-other-first-nations-people-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T15:01:21"
    },
    {
      "title": "Record strength El Niño could mean bigger supermarket bills for Australians, experts warn",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/08/record-strength-el-nino-could-mean-bigger-supermarket-bills-for-australians-experts-warn",
      "description": "<p>Predicted hot and dry weather in growing areas in eastern Australia identified as ‘one of the key issues’ that will affect food prices over next 12 months</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/08/barnaby-joyce-one-nation-superannuation-plan-john-howard-immigration-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The most severe El Niño weather event on record threatens to push food prices higher this year, experts say, piling pressure on households already struggling with the post-pandemic spike in grocery bills and complicating the Reserve Bank’s efforts to bring inflation back under control.</p><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/04/bom-forecasts-strongest-el-nino-on-record-as-research-points-to-alarming-climate-change-influence\">The Bureau of Meteorology has forecast</a> El Niño will peak in late spring or summer and “reach levels above the warmest observed since reliable records began in 1950”.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/sep/08/record-strength-el-nino-could-mean-bigger-supermarket-bills-for-australians-experts-warn\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T15:00:24"
    },
    {
      "title": "Grassroots Labor group urges Albanese government to chart course away from ‘American war machine’",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/grassroots-labor-pressure-group-albanese-government-us-military-war-machine",
      "description": "<p>Pressure follows revelations US military and weapons manufacturers control or have access to more than 100 bases across Australian continent</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/audio/2026/sep/07/why-can-the-us-access-so-many-australian-military-bases-and-could-they-drag-us-unwillingly-into-war-podcast\">Why can the US access so many Australian military bases? – podcast</a></p></li><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/08/barnaby-joyce-one-nation-superannuation-plan-john-howard-immigration-anthony-albanese-labor-angus-taylor-coalition-pauline-hanson-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The US has “led Australia into wars of aggression” for 50 years, internal party campaign group Labor Against War has argued, urging the government to chart a foreign policy independent “from the American war machine”.</p><p>The Australian government has defended the growing presence of the US military on the Australian continent, insisting the defence sites “are Australian bases under Australian control”, despite evidence the US military controls more than a dozen bases on Australian territory.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/08/grassroots-labor-pressure-group-albanese-government-us-military-war-machine\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-07T15:00:22"
    }
  ]
